WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.234
-Donald Trump apparently stashed
highly classified documents

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:05.667
about the nuclear capabilities

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.634
of a foreign nation
at his country club

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:10.868
and reportedly bragged
to friends he had intelligence

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.501
about the French president's
sex life.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.601
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:18.901
♪♪

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.234
Before we get to the story

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.334
about a deeply
compromised ex-president

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.501
with various connections
to international criminals

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:26.133
and shady financial
entanglements

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.968
who apparently stole
highly classified documents

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.200
about nuclear capabilities
and left them lying around

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.767
the basement
of his fake marble golf lair --

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.701
you know,
normal politics stuff --

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.000
there's also been
an intense heat wave

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.767
happening in California
and much of the West right now.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.234
Which, first of all, should be
yet another wake up call

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.234
to the imminent dangers
of climate change,

00:00:45.234 --> 00:00:46.968
but it's also
one of those stories

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.667
that comes along every so often
that neatly captures

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.200
just how craven and ghoulish
the modern GOP

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.434
has become under Donald Trump.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.534
You see, California Governor
Gavin Newsom

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.801
asked residents of the state
to conserve energy

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.667
for a few hours to avoid
blackouts,

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.067
and so far, it's worked.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.067
Californians banded together

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.434
and kept the power grid
running without issue.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:07.968
But then this mid-November
Jack-o-lantern

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.601
who sounds like Urkel
swallowed a kazoo

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.901
decided to chime in
on the whole thing

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.300
in a way that revealed
a complete lack of shame

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.200
and self-awareness
for no other reason

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.467
than he's apparently
just a glutton for humiliation.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:21.934
-I love that Gavin Newsom was
wearing his fleece,

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.701
obviously in cool air
conditioning,

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:27.467
saying, "Let them eat cake.
Let them sweat.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.200
You don't get air conditioning."

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.300
It's like John Kerry
who flies his private jet

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.167
all over the planet,
lecturing people

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.701
that you poor, gritty
working class

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.634
with dirt under
your fingernails,

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.234
you need to go
without an automobile.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.067
You need to turn
your air conditioner off.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:47.100
In fact, you need to just
stay home and eat worms.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.634
-Now, if he has worms
on the brain,

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:51.434
it's probably because
there was one in the bottle

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:54.200
of the tequila he drank in
Cancun after he fled his state

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.200
while his constituents froze
in a deadly winter storm.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.501
Do you guys remember that?
Is it bad?

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.934
Is it bad when your senator
looks like Harold Hill

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:03.434
trying to catch a train
out of town?

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:06.801
Now, aside from
the Cancun hypocrisy

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.734
from zombie Danny Zuko
over here,

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.968
I would also like to point out
that, unlike California,

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.834
Texas's deregulated power grid

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:17.000
actually did fail during that
deadly snowstorm in 2021,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.133
and remains so fragile
that Texas officials

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:23.334
basically did the same thing
as California earlier this year.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:26.868
Texas's grid operator urged
electricity conservation

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.334
as the heat wave
drove up demand.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:31.367
In fact, the state's
power grid operator asked Texans

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.634
to turn up their thermostats

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.667
and postpone
running major appliances

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:37.167
between 2:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.,
6 hours.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.267
That's just enough time
to book a flight to Cancun

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.434
and then have your neighbors,
who apparently all hate you,

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.634
rat you out to
"The New York Times."

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.100
Remember that?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.868
When Cruz invited his neighbors
to come to Cancun with him,

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.000
and instead, they immediately
called the newspapers

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.434
to complain about
how much of [bleep] he was.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:54.400
Imagine how much
you have to dislike

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.033
someone to call
a newspaper about it.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:03:00.267
I don't even know
how to call a newspaper.

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.501
What was that conversation?

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.567
"Man, Cruz stinks.
You gonna tweet about him?"

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.267
"No, I'm calling
the newspapers.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:08.200
I want every single person

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.267
staying at a hotel
to hear about this."

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:14.100
Anyway, Cruz is just one of
the more noxious examples

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.601
of the GOP's many shameless
liars and Trump toadies.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.801
There's also
Florida Senator Marco Rubio,

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:21.334
who has been one of Trump's
most vocal defenders

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.367
throughout the intensifying
criminal investigation

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.167
into all
the classified documents

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.968
Trump apparently
had stashed away

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.200
at his off-brand Marriott

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.100
for disbarred
personal injury lawyers.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.200
Rubio had already dismissed
the investigation

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.767
as a storage issue last week,

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:37.968
and now he's complaining
about leaks to the media.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.334
-If true, this "Washington Post"

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.834
report highly
classified documents

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:45.968
at Mar-a-Lago that only
a cabinet-level officer

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:48.367
or higher could even look at.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.834
That doesn't seem like
the kind of thing

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:55.400
you should have in your
post-presidential desk drawer.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.601
-Well, let's break this down.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:58.634
First of all, again,
we really don't know,

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.467
'cause let's go back
and understand

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.734
that all of this information

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:04.267
is coming from one side
and one place,

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:07.300
and that is sources with
knowledge of the investigation.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.534
Who are the sources with
knowledge of the investigation?

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:11.033
The FBI
and the Justice Department,

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.834
and they are leaking
to the media.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.667
And the only reason
to leak to the media

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.434
is to influence
the narrative,

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.234
which tells you
this is being politicized,

00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:19.801
which is doing damage
to the FBI,

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.033
the Justice Department,

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.868
to important institutions
to our country.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.234
-What do you think
does more damage

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.434
to our country's institution?

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:27.434
Leaking information about
an investigation

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.701
of a great public interest,

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.634
or Donald Trump bringing
home national secrets

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.667
on his last day
at work like Henry Winkler

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:35.868
taking home the Fonzie jacket
when they wrapped "Happy Days"?

00:04:35.868 --> 00:04:39.300
And I know the Fonzie jacket
is in the Smithsonian now,

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.100
but that's only after the Feds
raided Henry's house.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.367
Oh. Oh, he seems sweet,
ol' Henry Winkler,

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:47.167
but he almost
never leaves a room

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.400
without a stolen prop
in his pocket.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:56.167
But you know, I just have to say
I'm so surprised to hear

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.601
Rubio change his tune
on the Trump document scandal,

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:00.567
because before this
recent revelation,

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:03.634
he was actually very vocal about
the importance of being careful

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:05.100
with classified information.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.067
-Apparently, this is a level of
intelligence classification

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.367
that goes beyond top secret.

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:13.367
Now, am I wrong
in my reading of the law

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:16.667
that this would be
multiple felonies,

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:19.067
a felony in every case?

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.767
I mean, isn't this indictable?

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:24.701
-Yeah, this is very serious.
This is very serious.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.267
Number one, obviously,
there's a legal element to it.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.000
And again, we're going
to leave that to the FBI

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.400
and to the Justice Department.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.901
Yeah, but moving forward,
there's legal issues here.

00:05:32.901 --> 00:05:35.634
But let me just say, how can
the next commander in chief

00:05:35.634 --> 00:05:38.033
be someone
who inappropriately stashes

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.934
highly classified information?

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.567
-And the risk of that is?

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:44.100
-The risk of that is that
we're giving opponents

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.801
of this government
or adversaries

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.367
insight into our thinking,
into our decision making,

00:05:48.367 --> 00:05:50.100
and it provides
most certainly an advantage

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.701
in the national security realm.

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:53.000
-Thank you, Senator Rubio.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.834
Honestly, it's just
so refreshing to hear

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.534
a Republican finally muster up
the courage to state the obvious

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.868
and take on Trump's
various abuses of power.

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.968
In fact, to celebrate
his honesty and consistency,

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:05.167
we had an ice cream cake made
just for him that says on it,

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:08.634
"Thank you for your bravery,
Senator Rubio --"

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.133
Oh, crap. I forgot we...

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.901
We had to turn off
the fridge all day

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:13.901
to conserve power.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.334
Well, it's...

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.100
You guys, it's the thought.
It's the thought that counts.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.300
Anyway,
congratulations to Marco Rubio

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:21.501
for showing the courage --

00:06:21.501 --> 00:06:22.701
What's that?

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.767
The clips we showed
were from 2015 and 2016?

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.634
And he was talking about
Hillary Clinton's emails,

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.901
and we just edited out
the parts where he said her name

00:06:29.901 --> 00:06:32.200
to demonstrate the shameless
hypocrisy and self-debasement

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.234
in service of Donald Trump?

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:34.934
Well, then, you know what?

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:38.267
I'm glad the cake melted!

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:41.267
We'll just give it to the crew.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.834
Like, blend it up.

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:46.067
Tell them it's milkshakes.

00:06:46.067 --> 00:06:48.133
And let them know it's my idea.

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:51.334
Put a note on it
that says it from me.

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:54.734
That'll finally tap the brakes
on their bullying.

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.667 --> 00:07:01.133
Anyway.

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:03.033
So Rubio, like the rest of them,

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:05.033
continues to brush this off
like it's no big deal,

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:06.501
despite the fact that Trump

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:08.133
apparently had
some of the government's

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:10.100
most closely guarded secrets
in his possession,

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.167
which we now know
included materials

00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:14.434
about a foreign country's
nuclear capabilities.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.834
-We're following some
breaking news

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.067
on the Justice Department
investigation to the documents

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:19.400
Donald Trump had stashed away.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:21.100
"The Washington Post"
has just reported that,

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:25.634
"a document describing a foreign
government's military defenses,

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:27.834
including its
nuclear capabilities,

00:07:27.834 --> 00:07:29.300
was found by FBI agents

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.067
who searched Donald Trump's
Mar-a-Lago residence."

00:07:32.067 --> 00:07:34.567
The Post previously reported
that nuclear documents

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.734
were among those sought
by investigators.

00:07:36.734 --> 00:07:39.868
-Also from "The Post" reporting,
some of the seized documents

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:42.667
detail top secret
U.S. operations

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:44.033
that are so closely guarded,

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:46.133
many senior national
security officials

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.501
are kept in the dark about them.

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.133
-Okay, but in fairness,
Trump was probably

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:50.701
also kept
in the dark about them.

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:53.767
Technically, I guess they had
to show him classified documents

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:55.701
when he was president,
but they probably distracted him

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:57.100
the same way you gave your kid

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.200
an iPad on an airplane
to shut him up.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.133
"Alright, sir, here are those
nuclear documents

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:04.067
we are required
by law to show you.

00:08:04.067 --> 00:08:08.200
But also we DVR'd Rudy's latest
appearance on Hannity for you.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.734
You can watch that, or an
episode of 'Paw Patrol'."

00:08:10.734 --> 00:08:12.334
"Maybe. We do --

00:08:12.334 --> 00:08:17.100
We do love 'Paw Patrol.'
We love law and order.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:21.300
We love paws and laws and order.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:26.634
Plus, Rudy does kind of remind
me of Wally the Walrus."

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.534
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:30.167
Well, let's just take
a step back

00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:32.133
and let it soak in
how insane this is.

00:08:32.133 --> 00:08:35.000
The president just had a bunch
of highly classified materials

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:37.267
lying around the basement
of his country club

00:08:37.267 --> 00:08:39.067
about extremely
sensitive global affairs

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:41.367
that affect the safety and
security of the entire world.

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:43.367
And no, I'm not talking about

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:44.901
Harry Styles
spitting on Chris Pine,

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:48.701
although, although I will say
this right here is one of those

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:51.634
extremely rare pop culture
moments where I do wish

00:08:51.634 --> 00:08:54.501
Trump had his Twitter back,
just for a minute,

00:08:54.501 --> 00:08:57.467
so we could see what would
almost certainly be a psychotic

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.968
and likely very funny take
on the whole thing.

00:08:59.968 --> 00:09:03.000
"Many people are saying,
Harry No-Styles spit

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.300
(drooled?) on one of our
great American Chris's

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.334
at the Venus Film Festival.

00:09:08.334 --> 00:09:10.567
Could it have been
gum or mint (Tik Tak)?

00:09:10.567 --> 00:09:12.167
Lots of germs.

00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:14.067
Not nice!
Sleepy Joe should act!

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:16.734
#WheresHunterslaptop

00:09:16.734 --> 00:09:18.167
[ Applause ]

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:21.567
I would say the man knew how
to tweet, but he clearly didn't,

00:09:21.567 --> 00:09:23.167
and that's what
made it so special.

00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:25.400
I do think,
all things considered,

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.367
it's probably not ideal
that an ex-president

00:09:27.367 --> 00:09:29.033
with a bunch of corrupt
foreign entanglements

00:09:29.033 --> 00:09:30.167
to mobsters and dictators,

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.467
not to mention various
indicted henchmen,

00:09:32.467 --> 00:09:34.400
had a bunch of classified
information about weapons

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.434
that could eliminate
all life on earth

00:09:36.434 --> 00:09:37.868
just lying around
his country club

00:09:37.868 --> 00:09:41.100
where spies or Botox salesmen
could just easily find them.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.801
But don't you worry.

00:09:42.801 --> 00:09:46.667
Trump's very normal son, Eric,
would like to assure us,

00:09:46.667 --> 00:09:49.367
contrary to the photo
the Justice Department released

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:51.100
as part of its affidavit
in the case,

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.934
Trump kept his country club
very organized.

00:09:53.934 --> 00:09:55.534
-You literally have the FBI

00:09:55.534 --> 00:09:58.634
spending more time
leaking stuff to the press.

00:09:58.634 --> 00:10:00.834
I mean, these pictures --
you think my father happened

00:10:00.834 --> 00:10:03.200
to just leave documents
all over his office floor?

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.601
-No, I think when
the FBI found them,

00:10:05.601 --> 00:10:08.934
they laid them out
and took a picture of them.

00:10:08.934 --> 00:10:12.234
I also don't think drug dealers
keep all their money and cocaine

00:10:12.234 --> 00:10:13.767
neatly stacked on one table.

00:10:13.767 --> 00:10:15.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:17.434
"Hey, you sure we shouldn't hide
this stuff somewhere, boss?"

00:10:17.434 --> 00:10:20.868
"Nah, I like the way
it brings the room together.

00:10:20.868 --> 00:10:24.734
Yeah, make them neat.
Make all the money neat."

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:26.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.868 --> 00:10:29.367
Also, I love how these guys
suddenly complain about leaks

00:10:29.367 --> 00:10:30.934
now, after supporting
Donald Trump,

00:10:30.934 --> 00:10:33.567
arguably the biggest and
messiest gossip on the planet.

00:10:33.567 --> 00:10:36.167
He reportedly bragged to
some of his closest associates,

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:37.834
both during and after his time
in the White House,

00:10:37.834 --> 00:10:40.100
that he knew illicit details
about the love life

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.801
of French President
Emmanuel Macron.

00:10:41.801 --> 00:10:44.267
I'm sorry,
you think it's scandalous

00:10:44.267 --> 00:10:47.734
that a French politician
had an illicit love life?

00:10:47.734 --> 00:10:49.300
You know what would be
way more scandalous?

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:52.100
A French politician
with a boring love life.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:53.400
You think an illicit love life

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.701
would be bad for
Emmanuel Macron?

00:10:54.701 --> 00:10:56.467
I'm pretty sure
his official campaign slogan

00:10:56.467 --> 00:10:58.667
was Macron a trois?

00:10:58.667 --> 00:10:59.934
[ Laughter ]

00:10:59.934 --> 00:11:02.801
There's no simpler,
more straightforward example

00:11:02.801 --> 00:11:04.534
of how brazen and shameless
the Republican Party

00:11:04.534 --> 00:11:06.400
has become in its acceptance
of lawbreaking

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.100
and abuses of power
when it comes to Donald Trump.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.601
They will support or apologize
for anything he does,

00:11:10.601 --> 00:11:13.067
no matter how egregious,
because they are fully in thrall

00:11:13.067 --> 00:11:14.434
to his authoritarian cult.

00:11:14.434 --> 00:11:15.601
When it comes to Trump,

00:11:15.601 --> 00:11:17.267
guys like Ted Cruz
and Marco Rubio

00:11:17.267 --> 00:11:18.367
have the spines of...

00:11:18.367 --> 00:11:20.267
-Worms.

00:11:20.267 --> 00:11:22.834
[ Laughter ]

